--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -270,28 +270,24 @@ docs/
 ## Where the contract comes from
 
 ```
-confflow config contract --json   ──┐
-                                    ├─► ProducerContractProvider ─► strict parse
-V2 stable-fallback snapshot      ──┘        (verified digests)        │
-                                                                      ▼
-                                                        VerifiedEditorContract
-                                                                      │
-                                          EditorContractService.current()
-                                                                      │
-                                                        WorkflowEditorService ─► pages
+confflow config contract --json (over SSH) ─► V4 strict parse (verified digests)
+                                                         │
+                                                         ▼
+                                              V4ContractService.current()
+                                                         │
+                                            WorkflowEditorService ─► pages
 ```
 
-Set `JOBDESK_V2_CONTRACT=/path/to/contract.json` to resolve a real producer
-contract at start-up. If it is absent, unreadable or fails digest verification,
-V2 runs on its bundled snapshot and the New Run page says which of the two is in
-force. Pages never see producer bytes, never check a hash and never choose to
-fall back — that all happens in `application/editor/contract/`, and
-`tests/application/test_architecture.py` enforces it.
-
-Against an older ConfFlow that publishes only the v1 contract, V2 enters a
-**compatibility / restricted mode**: the stable fallback field model is used,
-this is stated on screen, and the Run action stays disabled. An old producer is
-never silently treated as fully compatible.
+Until a server contract resolves, the editor holds `NoContract`: configuration
+editing is disabled and the New Run page says so. Pages never see producer
+bytes, never check a hash and never choose to fall back — that all happens in
+`application/editor/contract/`, and `tests/application/test_architecture.py`
+enforces it.
+
+Against an older ConfFlow that publishes only the v1 contract, V2 refuses it
+with a structured diagnostic stated on screen; configuration editing and the
+Run action stay disabled. An old producer is never silently treated as
+compatible.
 
 ## Contributing rules (not suggestions)
 
