-"""Where a contract comes from.
-
-A provider answers one question: *given a target, what contract should the
-application use?*  It is the only place that knows whether a producer was
-reachable, and the only place that decides to fall back.  Everything downstream
-sees a :class:`VerifiedEditorContract` and cannot tell the difference -- which is
-the point, because "the producer is down" is an infrastructure fact, not a
-feature the GUI should have to branch on.
-
-Two providers live here:
-
-:class:`StableFallbackContractProvider`
-    Always resolves the bundled, version-pinned snapshot.  This is what V2 runs
-    on today, because ConfFlow does not publish an editor manifest yet.
-:class:`LocalProducerContractProvider`
-    Reads producer bytes from a filesystem location and verifies them.  On any
-    failure -- missing file, bad encoding, bad digest, unknown version -- it
-    degrades to its fallback **and keeps the error as a diagnostic**, so the
-    reason is visible instead of the failure being swallowed.
-
-The remote fetch is not here: it needs a transport port, so it has a module of
-its own.  See :mod:`.remote_v4`, whose
-:class:`~.remote_v4.V4ProducerContractProvider` runs the one contract command
-over a :class:`~jobdesk_v2.application.remote.RemoteCommandRunner`, dispatches
-the V4 envelope, and degrades on exactly the same terms.
-
-Degradation never loses information.  A degraded contract is a real contract --
-same invariants, same capability model -- with the producer's error attached, so
-a page can show "using compatibility fallback: the producer contract ..." rather
-than silently showing a stale field set.
-
-**The application layer does not read files (R13).**  A provider that resolved a
-local location used to call ``Path.read_bytes`` itself, which put a filesystem
-call inside ``application`` and made the layering gate either lie or be weakened.
-It now takes a :class:`ContractByteSource` -- a one-method port -- and parses the
-bytes it is handed.  ``application`` decides *what to do with* producer bytes;
-``infrastructure`` decides how a path becomes bytes.
-"""
